From 09effe171649aa93e723d5296b571a13c8f51ed1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan Hertenberger <erde74@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 11:14:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 52/59] ape: setvbuf with no buffer and size 0 allocates BUFSIZ

setvbuf(f, nil, _IOFBF or _IOLBF, 0), asking stdio to choose the
buffer, did malloc(0) and set bufl 0: the writes then went past the
block of no bytes into the heap (SDL's driver does this). Now BUFSIZ,
the size stdio takes itself.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sys/src/ape/lib/ap/stdio/setvbuf.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sys/src/ape/lib/ap/stdio/setvbuf.c b/sys/src/ape/lib/ap/stdio/setvbuf.c
index 58bea0098..496f316cd 100644
--- a/sys/src/ape/lib/ap/stdio/setvbuf.c
+++ b/sys/src/ape/lib/ap/stdio/setvbuf.c
@@ -14,6 +14,12 @@ int setvbuf(FILE *f, char *buf, int mode, size_t size){
 		f->flags|=LINEBUF;
 	case _IOFBF:
 		if(buf==0){
+			/*
+			 * no buffer and no size: one of the size stdio takes
+			 * (malloc(0), a buffer of no bytes, the writes ran past)
+			 */
+			if(size==0)
+				size=BUFSIZ;
 			buf=malloc(size);
 			if(buf==0){
 				f->state=ERR;
